ASPIRATIONAL: the runtime interpreter is deferred pending a rewrite.

Ruled 2026-06-25 (Lars). The interpreter was built early as an experiment, not
as a cornerstone feature, and the language has moved so far since that the whole
subsystem needs a rewrite rather than incremental repair:

  - the execution/budgeting model predates the current obligation + effect design
    (see 410_BUDGETED_INTERPRETER, also deferred),
  - it carries its OWN separate parser (430_002_parser_userland,
    430_047_runtime_run_parse_error) that needs to be rebuilt against the
    current grammar.

So the entire 430_RUNTIME category is marked aspirational — deferred wholesale,
NOT cherry-picked. Greens here are coincidental partial coverage; reds are the
rewrite's to-do list, not active failures.

Transparency note (so nothing is silently buried): 430_020_interpreter_if_e2e
is a PARKED REGRESSION — it was green and broke at commit 20f70961. It is not an
aspirational gap; it is a real green→red that this deferral parks until the
interpreter rewrite. Surface it again when the rewrite begins.
